---
id: RS-005
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: todo!() or unimplemented!() shipped
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '\b(?:todo|unimplemented)!\s*[\(\[\{]'

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A `todo!()` / `unimplemented!()` macro panics the moment a caller reaches it —
shipping one is a runtime abort waiting to happen. Finish the implementation, or
return a real error and open a ticket for the gap.

This is a regex rule (the macro is unambiguous on its own line), so unlike the
rest of the family it is not `#[cfg(test)]`-aware; suppress deliberate
test-scaffolding stubs with `// @anvil-ignore RS-005 -- test stub`.
